  2	 * Scoped to two CodeRabbit PR review findings on this component, not full coverage of every
  3	 * branch (order price adjustments, coupon items, tax, cart items, promo code form) — see
  4	 * `.claude/rules/testing.md`'s no-duplicate-coverage rule for why a component test should assert
  5	 * only its own contract:
  6	 *
  7	 *  1. Shipping promotions are aggregated from every `basket.shippingItems` entry, not just
  8	 *     `shippingItems[0]` — a multi-shipment basket can have a promotion on shipment 2+.
  9	 *  2. `shippingTotal` renders "Free" at 0, the formatted value when a real number, and "TBD"
 10	 *     when null/undefined, mirroring the existing `taxTotal` pattern.
 11	 *
 12	 * `usePromoCode`/`PromoCode`, `../icons`, and a few `CartItems`-only sub-imports are mocked at
 13	 * the smallest surface, none of it relevant to the two findings under test:
 14	 *  - `usePromoCode` internally calls `useCurrentBasket()`, which needs the full commerce
 15	 *    provider stack for no reason relevant here — this component receives its own `basket` as a
 16	 *    prop, and `usePromoCode`'s internal basket only feeds the promo-code *form*, which
 17	 *    `showPromoCodeForm` defaults to hidden.
 18	 *  - `../icons` re-exports the base SFCC icons barrel, which throws under Vitest (see
 19	 *    testing.md's known gap) — the same class of fix documented at footer/index.test.tsx.
 20	 *  - `link`, `item-variant/item-name`, and `item-variant/item-attributes` (base SFCC files —
 21	 *    `link` is used directly for the "Edit cart" button, the other two only ever render inside
 22	 *    `CartItems`, which this suite never enables via `showCartItems`) pull in
 23	 *    `use-multi-site`/`use-currency`, which import `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/contexts`
 24	 *    directly — a `.js` file containing raw JSX Vite's default `.js` loader can't parse (Vite
 25	 *    only applies the JSX parser to `.jsx`/`.tsx` by default; Storybook's webpack config papers
 26	 *    over this with an explicit babel-loader rule, but `vitest.config.ts` is Tier 1/frozen and
 27	 *    not this suite's to change). The static `import` at the top of index.tsx pulls these in
 28	 *    regardless of whether `CartItems` ever renders, so mocking is required even though this
 29	 *    suite's own assertions never touch them.
 30	 *  - `promo-popover` uses Chakra's `Popover` with `trigger="hover"` — its content is `isLazy`
 31	 *    and only mounts on hover, and it separately imports the same base icons barrel as above.
